  "result": "Based on my search of the codebase, I found the invitation refusal logic for seat limit enforcement.\n\nIn `src/invites.ts`, the `inviteMember` function checks if an organization has exhausted its seat allocation. It retrieves the maximum seats allowed for the organization's plan tier from `src/limits.ts`, and if `org.seatsUsed >= limits.maxSeats`, it throws a `SeatLimitError`, refusing the invitation.\n\nThe function explicitly states in its comment: \"Refuses an invitation once the organization has consumed every seat its plan allows. This is the seat-cap enforcement point.\"\n\nBoth files are involved in this decision:\n- `src/invites.ts` contains the refusal logic\n- `src/limits.ts` provides the plan tier limits that define the maximum seats available\n\nANSWER: src/invites.ts, src/limits.ts",
